#: includes/class-gateway.php:187
msgid "Migration / legacy compatibility"
msgstr "Migration / Altkompatibilität"

#: includes/class-gateway.php:189
msgid ""
"Options for stores migrating from the previous Briqpay for WooCommerce "
"plugin."
msgstr "Optionen für Shops, die vom vorherigen Plugin Briqpay for WooCommerce migrieren."

#: includes/class-gateway.php:192
msgid "Legacy B2B order meta mapping"
msgstr "Alte Meta-Zuordnung für B2B-Bestellungen"

#: includes/class-gateway.php:193
msgid "Also store B2B order data using the previous plugin's meta keys"
msgstr "B2B-Bestelldaten zusätzlich in den Meta-Schlüsseln des vorherigen Plugins speichern"

#: includes/class-gateway.php:195
msgid ""
"For stores migrating from the previous Briqpay plugin. B2B orders "
"additionally store the organisation number in <code>_billing_org_nr</code> "
"and the shipping email in <code>_shipping_email</code>, so existing ERP "
"exports and integrations keep working. Current meta keys are always written "
"as well."
msgstr "Für Shops, die vom vorherigen Briqpay-Plugin migrieren. B2B-Bestellungen speichern die Handelsregisternummer zusätzlich in <code>_billing_org_nr</code> und die E-Mail-Adresse der Lieferanschrift in <code>_shipping_email</code>, damit bestehende ERP-Exporte und Integrationen weiterhin funktionieren. Die aktuellen Meta-Schlüssel werden immer ebenfalls geschrieben."

